size == 0`), which is fine to hijack. Libraries like `github.com/coder/websocket` write headers and then hijack. So does middleware that calls `WriteHeaderNow()` or `Flush()` first. That second case was failing.\n\n**Changes:**\n- **`response_writer.go`:** `Hijack()` now checks `w.size > 0` instead of `w.Written()`, and has a comment explaining why. The error message now reads `\"gin: response body already written\"`.\n- **`response_writer_test.go`:** added cases to `TestResponseWriterHijackAfterWrite`:\n  - hijacking after `WriteHeader(101)` + `WriteHeaderNow()` succeeds\n  - hijacking after `Flush()` succeeds\n  - hijacking after `WriteString` fails with `errHijackAlreadyWritten`, alongside the existing `Write` case\n\nYou're on a detached HEAD. Want me to create a branch and commit this as `fix(response): refine hijack behavior for response lifecycle`?","ttft_ms":4547,"type":"result","duration_ms":27877,"uuid":"0ab21d08-853e-46d2-ae5f-fe08282e9e0b","ttft_stream_ms":885,"time_to_request_ms":137,"first_content_frame_ms":885,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
